Ladybird snaps a box at the end of every gesture whose input scrolled
it, including input the compositor applied in the same update that
reported the end of an earlier snap scroll of the box. Blink does the
same: Its InputHandler::ScrollEnd() calls SnapAtScrollEnd() with
SnapReason::kGestureScrollEnd when a gesture ends, which snaps from the
box’s current offset — and its comment covers a gesture that arrives
while the box is still snapping for an earlier one.

WebKit’s ScrollingEffectsController::processWheelEventForScrollSnap()
starts a snap animation from the current offset on UserScrollEnd. And
Gecko’s AsyncPanZoomController::OnScrollWheel() snaps the delta of each
wheel event, in MaybeAdjustDeltaForScrollSnappingOnWheelInput().
